			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2774778">
									

<p>I like the historical approach, the first two tabs were an excellent setup, but the third blew it for me. I anticipated, and really did look forward to the Cousin Johnny connection, but the actions taken by the affected weren't enough to differentiate itself from that horror-wise. I probably could have overlooked that if it weren't for the ending.</p>
<p>SIGHTSEE is a cool concept, but I feel like the (in-universe) author's interpretations of its intentions and role came across as pure exposition. I think you could have led the reader around to the implication that it <em>is</em> the one true God more naturally. This aspect, moreso than the similarities to 2852, is what led to my downvote. I think that's an avenue of horror that's not being explored by, well, any of the other entries (to my knowledge), and would have done a great deal set this apart from the pack.</p>

							</div>

								
					
